      "curator_note": "adduct corrected to null (convention G): the species undergoing this reaction is an EVEN-ELECTRON cation (charge +1, radical_electrons 0) - a fragment/secondary-fragmentation precursor - NOT the [M]+. radical molecular ion. Even-electron cyclobutyl cation undergoing retro-[2+2] with charge RETENTION: cleaving the two ring bonds gives the vinyl cation CH2=CH+ (charge kept on the original cationic carbon C2) + neutral ethylene. Book draws 4 fishhook barbs (a two-barbed mark on each cleaved vertical ring bond, left Cc-Ca=<1,3> and right Cb-Cd=<2,4>). For this even-electron charge-retention path the cleavage is heterolytic, so it is encoded as two DOUBLE-barbed moves (<1,3> pair -> C1=C2 pi; <2,4> pair -> C3=C4 pi) rather than four single fishhooks; the book's fishhook glyphs literally depict the competing homolytic (unfavored) reading, see 4.6e."
